    "narrative": "For the 2026-07-02 slate, **Jonathan Aranda** stands as our premier offensive anchor. With a robust score of 70.47, he benefits from a perfect storm of environmental and tactical advantages: he\u2019s slotted into the #2 hole, holds a significant platoon advantage against Kolek, and is bolstered by favorable wind conditions blowing out. While **Bryson Stott** (62.94) and **Masyn Winn** (60.61) also clear the 60-point threshold for strong starts, they trail **Jonathan Aranda** primarily due to the latter\u2019s superior lineup position and projected xwOBA. **Masyn Winn** remains a high-upside play, as the matchup against the struggling Waldrep (7.82 xERA) provides the highest SP skill boost on the board, offering a favorable environment for him to produce despite a lower batting order placement.\n\nThe bench decisions today were largely dictated by external factors rather than performance dips, though **Cal Raleigh** (57.53) and **Gavin Sheets** (57.49) sit right on the edge of our starting threshold. **Cal Raleigh** was considered for a demotion to the bench to preserve our game cap, but his raw power ceiling against Ure\u00f1a kept him in the C1 slot. Meanwhile, we continue to manage the absence of key assets like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** due to IL stints, forcing us to lean on depth pieces like **Gavin Sheets** to bridge the gap. Looking ahead, we need to monitor the availability of **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Taylor Ward**, as their future integration will be vital once we move beyond the current period of player inactivity for names like **Lawrence Butler** and **Geraldo Perdomo**. With **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Drew Gilbert** currently occupying roster space, the focus remains on identifying daily platoon edges to maximize our 5x5 production while staying vigilant on weather risks that could dampen output for our bottom-tier starters.",
